; ===========================================================================
; pi-system — OPTIONAL local npm cache (Verdaccio) opt-in
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Written into a project's frontend by:  ./scripts/new-project.sh ... --cache
; (or copy this file there yourself). It points npm at the platform's local
; Verdaccio cache, which transparently proxies + caches the public npm registry.
;
; This is a HARD opt-in: while this file is present, npm WILL use the cache, so
; the cache must be running (./scripts/cache.sh up) AND reachable from wherever
; the install runs — i.e. on the `internal` Docker network (see docs/README.md
; "Package cache" for the build-network note). To stop using the cache and fall
; back to the public npm registry, simply DELETE this file.
;
; Prefer GRACEFUL auto-fallback over a committed file? Don't use this .npmrc —
; instead set the env var only when you want the cache, e.g.:
;     npm_config_registry=http://verdaccio:4873/ npm ci
; (unset => npm uses the public registry automatically).
; ===========================================================================
registry=http://verdaccio:4873/
